The Solidity contracts in contracts/ carry an MIT SPDX header.
AttestationRegistry, CuratorSet and CuratorSetRegistry are copied unchanged
from noorchain-core, by the same copyright holder. PeriodRegistry is derived
from noorchain-core's PoSSRegistry, and the signature loop of
ThresholdSignatures follows the one in PoSSRegistry.

Code that this repository takes from the curators-hub and foundation
applications of noorchain-core is placed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
by the same copyright holder. Each package that holds such code lists, in its
LISEZMOI.md, the files it takes and what was changed.

A complete reviewer package built by scripts/paquet-reviseur/construire.mjs
(CT-8 §13) redistributes dist/ethers.js from the npm distribution of ethers,
under the MIT license, together with its LICENSE.md.

The noortrace-verifier binary built from verificateur/ (CT-6 §14) contains
code from the Go standard library and runtime (BSD-3-Clause, with PATENTS),
golang.org/x/crypto (BSD-3-Clause, with PATENTS) and
github.com/decred/dcrd/dcrec/secp256k1/v4 (ISC). Their license notices are
reproduced in verificateur/LICENCES-TIERCES, which is distributed with every
published binary.
